  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a user who gets an error or a question, I want the alert's title to say what failed or what is asked, so that I understand it without reading the whole message.\n\n### Rule\n\n\"Write a title that clearly and succinctly describes the situation. […] As much as possible, describe what happened, the context in which it happened, and why. Avoid writing a title that doesn't convey useful information — like \"Error\" or \"Error 329347 occurred\"\" — [HIG › Alerts](https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/alerts) (Content; page updated 2024-02-02).\n\n### What the app does (dev-swift @ `7a61018f`)\n\n- « Erreur »: `App/SwiftHFR/Settings/PseudoListEditorView.swift:64`.\n- « Icône » (an icon change that failed): `App/SwiftHFR/Settings/AppIconSettingsView.swift:49`, `Settings/AppIconSeasonModel.swift:110-111`.\n- « Action impossible »: `Accounts/AccountsView.swift:68`, `Accounts/AccountMenuButton.swift:64`, `Messages/MessageListView.swift:81-82`, `Messages/ReaderMarkUnreadFlow.swift:64`, `Navigation/TopicListView.swift:118-119`.\n- « Stockage MP » for two different questions: `MPStorage/BlocklistSyncQuestions.swift:15`, `Reader/Actions/ReaderBookmarkFlow.swift:12`.\n\nOther alerts in the same code do it right (« Alerte impossible », « Notifications désactivées dans iOS »).\n\n### Legacy at `87fe0d1c`\n\n`HFRswift/Swift/AppSettingsView.swift:735` (and `:632`): `.alert(\"Erreur\", …)` on the same list editor; `Classes/MPStorage.m:91`, `:849`: title « Stockage MP ». Legacy's delete failure is specific (« Suppression impossible », `MessagesView.swift:5529`).\n\n### Class\n\n**(b) evolution, M5** (wording, mostly shared with legacy).\n\n### Proposed fix and check\n\n- Title each alert with what failed or what is asked: « Ajout impossible » / « Suppression impossible », « Changement d'icône impossible », « Changement de compte impossible », « Synchroniser la liste noire ? », « Activer le stockage MP ? »; the detail stays in the message. One pass with the button-title issue of this review (#1151).\n- Check: text review of the titles; no rendering needed.\n\nFound by #866 (cloud/r866-fable, Fable 5.2)",
